-- Migration 103: Complete shapes for the Fall Hiking Spree's trails (spec 050)
--
-- Seven of the spree's trails were drawn without the stretches they share with
-- another trail (Seneca without its Nuthatch section, Adam Run without Spring
-- Hollow's, ...), so none of them closed into the loop a hiker walks. "Parcours
-- Trail" was worse: one place holding two trails of that name, in Goodyear
-- Heights and in Sand Run, nine kilometres apart.
--
-- Each is replaced by Summit Metro Parks' own line for the whole named trail,
-- from the district's public "SMP Trails by Name" layer on ArcGIS Online,
-- retrieved October 2026. Parcours Trail keeps the Goodyear Heights trail (the
-- one on the spree) and the Sand Run trail becomes a place of its own.
--
-- Runs on every boot. Each UPDATE matches only the incomplete shape it
-- replaces, by its length, so a trail redrawn since is left alone.

